{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Controlling the Story", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Miranda at the Press Conference", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Exchange information about people's interests and backgrounds using a wider range of language.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Using the Conditional 'if-then' Construction in Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "Probing questions try to get at deep understandings of an issue. The conditional construction can be useful for this. When one fact depends on another fact to be true, then we use the 'if-then' construction.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We may be told something that we are not sure that we believe because of something else we have heard or experienced. We may express each idea in a clause, making one dependent on the other. You know one thing is true, so the other one is false unless someone has some information that is not obvious.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: Something you heard doesn't seem to make sense because of something you observed. Is what you heard wrong, or is there more information that is missing?", "type": "text"}, {"content": " <span class=\"italic\"><ol>1. You have heard that your colleague is quitting his job.</ol><ol>2. You observe your colleague put more money on his cafeteria lunch card, as if he were staying longer.</ol></span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Probing Question: If he is quitting his job, then why did he put more money on his cafeteria lunch card?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are two sides to your question. One is asked, but the second, unasked question, is <span class=\"underline\">what you really want to know</span> most. <br /><ol>1. Asked: <span class=\"italic\">Why did he put money on his card?</span></ol><ol>2. Unasked: <span class=\"italic\">Is he really quitting?</span> Maybe he isn't!", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Most likely it is NOT true that your colleague is quitting. But there may be information you don't know about. For instance, perhaps he is going to gift his meal card to another colleague when he leaves.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Statement you don't know if you believe\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Something you do know\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Probing question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"There is a real Santa Claus who gives gifts to all children in one night.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Gifts for all the children in the world couldn't all fit in Santa's sleigh.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">If</span> Santa Claus gives gifts to all the children in the world on one night, <span class=\\\"underline\\\">then how</span> do they all fit in his sleigh?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Our manager is doing a fantastic job.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Many good employees are leaving.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">If</span> our manager is doing a fantastic job, <span class=\\\"underline\\\">then why</span> are so many good employees leaving?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"My husband said he bought me flowers.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"My husband walked home and he is not carrying flowers.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"underline\\\">If</span> he bought me flowers but isn't carrying them, <span class=\\\"underline\\\">then  where</span> did he put them?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<br />Often in spoken English, we leave out the word \u201cthen\u201d. It is understood without being said.<br/><br/> *The clauses of these questions can be turned around. Just remember that the indefinite pronouns should be replaced by the specific nouns in the first clause.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">If</span> Santa Claus gives gifts to all the children in the world on one night, <span class=\"underline\">how</span> do they all fit in his sleigh?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">If</span> our manager is doing a fantastic job, <span class=\"underline\">why</span> are so many good employees leaving?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">If</span> he bought me flowers but isn't carrying them, <span class=\"underline\">where</span> did he put them?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How do all the gifts fit in Santa Claus's sleigh, if he gives them to all the children in the world on one night?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Why are so many good employees leaving, if our manager is doing a fantastic job?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Where did he put the flowers, if he bought me some?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Dealing with Challenging and Hostile Questions", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are times when you may be asked questions which are hostile or difficult to answer. Using polite, honest answers helps keep everyone calm even when the questioner wishes to raise emotions.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Sometimes questions are not meant as questions at all - they could be intended to make you look unprepared, to confuse you, or give a negative message to you and other listeners. One approach to answering hostile questions is to <span class=\"underline\">ask for a chance to explain</span>. This gives you a chance to gather your thoughts and prevent the other person from interrupting you before you get to provide a thoughtful answer.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Examples: <br />May I explain? <br />May I proceed without interruption? <br />May I continue? <br />Please allow me to explain. <br />Will you allow me to go on?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Another important tip is to <span class=\"underline\">acknowledge the person's question</span>, no matter how rude or uncomfortable the question. <span class=\"underline\">Then continue to say what you really feel is important</span> to communicate.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">HostiIe question</span>: If you are an honest company, how can you buy products from that horrible business? <br /><span class=\"underline\">Response</span>: We are honest (<span class=\"underline\">acknowledgment</span>) and we will encourage that company to change its practices if they want our business (<span class=\"underline\">your main point</span>).<br /><br />", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Hostile question</span>: You didn't care to recycle for ten years, right? <br /><span class=\"underline\">Response</span>: We did not recycle for a long time (<span class=\"underline\">acknowledgment of question</span>) and are happy to announce that we have learned to do differently (<span class=\"underline\">your main point</span>).<br /><br />", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Hostile question</span>: Why don't you give your employees job security with long-term contracts? <br /><span class=\"underline\">Response</span>: We are not giving out long-term contracts (<span class=\"underline\">acknowledgment</span>) until we know whether or not we will be successful enough in this area to give people job security (<span class=\"underline\">your main point</span>).", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "overview", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a short summary of the main points", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Miranda, would you give us an overview of this situation?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use in a meeting.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "private investigator", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone hired by a company or individual to find out secret information", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  We found the real facts with a private investigator.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob10aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ethical stand", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a strong public decision about what is right or wrong and act according to that decision", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Now this is common and legal in Tindasia, but we have a strong ethical stand against child labor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "interruption", "type": "name"}, {"content": "stopping someone's speech by saying something; something that breaks the flow", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  It would be clearer if I could explain without interruption.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob10aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "follow up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do something that builds on or adds to a previous action ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  We found a rumor over social media and immediately followed up with an investigation.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob10aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to proceed", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to move forward", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  May I proceed?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of a situation that you know something about but don't have enough information on to really understand the truth.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create probing questions using \"if ... then ...\"", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Once you have a list of 4-5 questions, exchange your list with your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Answer the questions by acknowledging them politely and providing necessary information.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I ask probing questions about an issue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "My partner and I exchange our ideas.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I answer probing questions politely and in detail.", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le09ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can ask probing questions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk about jobs and work.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can deal with challenging and hostile questions.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What do you think the term \u201cprobing question\u201d means?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "What are some strategies to deal with hostile questions?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Is it an honest company?", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Miranda is interviewed by a reporter. What  a <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">distressing</span> situation!", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}]}, {"content": [{"content": "<span class = \"italic\">\u201cDistressing\u201d</span> means worrying/terrible.", "tip_id": 0, "type": "text"}], "type": "tips"}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Click on the play button to listen to the audio.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 1, "stimuli_ids": [1]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "MT1", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "if there is a chance to make things clear?", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "Miranda, would you give us an overview of this situation,", "type": "text"}]}, {"content": "secondary_1", "type": "objective"}], "id": 0}, {"responses": [{"correc